From: Rhnn Hur <hurrhnn@icmp.kr>
Subject: [PATCH] luci-app-airoha-flowsense: support AN7563

AN7563 (AN7552 die, e.g. ipTIME BE5100M; OpenWrt subtarget
airoha/an7563). The package Makefile applies this patch only for
that subtarget, so the code assumes an AN7563 and does not detect the
SoC at run time.

- devmem is read-only and limited to a fixed whitelist (PSE, GDM1/GDM2,
  CDM1/CDM2, PLL 0x1fa202ac/0x1fa202b8). Reads happen only while
  airoha_eth / airoha-eth is bound, because reading an unclocked block
  can hang the bus. GDM3 and GDM4 are never read.
- PLL readback uses the AN7552 decode: PCW 0x1fa202ac[31:24], POSDIV
  0x1fa202b8[20:18]. pll_valid tells the UI whether the value is real.
- The NPU firmware is found through the firmware-name of any npu@* DT
  node instead of the fixed EN7581 file name, with fallbacks.
- JSON API: getStatus adds pll_valid and eth_bound. getFrameEngine
  drops gdm4 and returns {"error": ...} while the Ethernet driver is
  not bound.
- The UI shows the two Wi-Fi bands of the MT7992 (no 6 GHz); its
  5 GHz radio is 3SS EHT160 (4323 Mbps).
- The PSE walk covers 11 ports, like the stock fe_core.
- npu_cores no longer prints a second "0" when there is no NPU.

This patch is applied only when building for the airoha/an7563
subtarget (see the package Makefile).
